11

Curriculum: 24 
META24’s overarching goal is to promote the use of higher level thinking 
skills as students master both foundational and challenging skills.
META-COGNITION
The use of higher-level thinking skills provides development and practice in problem-
solving and leads to metacognition. Students not only know what they have learned 
but know how they have learned it.
The underlying framework for this form of studying is the Inquiry Bridge curriculum model. It serves as a roadmap 
for  both  teachers  and  students  as  they  move  together  through  24  separate  but  interrelated  skill  clusters.  As  
they  proceed,  a  colorful,  computerized  Success  Board  plots  individual  student  progress  which  aids  students  in  
monitoring and reinforcing their progress. The continuously updated Success Board also helps instructors monitor 
students’ responses in order to provide timely feedback.
12

13
PROGRESS MONITORING
Teachers  access  the  LMS  to  monitor  student  progress  and  plan  instructional  
interventions  when  necessary.  Teachers  and  administrators  are  able  to  aggregate  
data in the LMS to evaluate the overall progress being achieved within the Inquiry Bridge curriculum by grade level, 
content subject, and schoolwide filters.
The Learning Management System is developed to incorporate essential features required to  advance students 
at an accelerated rate. Synthesized standards assist students by filling in the gaps so that they may be successful 
in competently completing the most challenging coursework which ultimately develops their higher-level thinking 
skills. Additionally, students’ confidence and knowledge base are increased as newly acquired learning strategies 
are developed and honed through repeated practice and increased difficulty.
Learning Managment System
LMS
Student data is collected on the Success Board and is displayed through a Learning Management 
System (LMS). While many learning management systems collect data and provide instructional 
links to lesson plans, the LMS used in the METALAB is much more robust. This LMS provides four separate but 
interconnected sections.
The  LMS  provides  parents  with  information  pertaining  to  the  assignments  and  progress  of  their  students.    It  
also  provides  information  about  community  projects,  especially  those  in  which  students  and  members  of  the  
community work collaboratively. 
The  LMS  provides  professional  development  for  teachers  to  reinforce  their  teaching  techniques,  especially  in  
differentiating instruction while maximizing the impact of inquiry-based instruction.  
The  LMS  provides  the  students  a  section  with  a  comprehensive  combination  of  lessons,  reviews,  placement  
assessments,  practice  quizzes,  and  mastery  tests.  Students  interact  daily  with  the  LMS  to  keep  track  of  their  
assignments, practice skills, review steps, watch instructional videos, and take their unit assessments. Students 
also access the LMS to post learning blogs and monitor their progress throughout the units.

