MAKE IT HAPPEN
META24  learning  centers  educate  public  school  students.  The  centers  are  funded  
through a variety of methods including district-paid tuition, state aid/grants, federal aid/
grants, private foundations and individual philanthropists. Although educating public school students often with 
public funds, META24 centers are privately run by the META division of Banner Learning Corp, a nonprofit 501(c)
(3) organization. 
Being  operated  by  a  private  nonprofit  organization  results  in  greater  freedom  to  implement  our  innovative  and  
highly effective educational methods. These methods often lead to significantly greater success among students. 
At the same time, we operate the learning centers in conformance with any applicable district, state, and federal 
education standards. Moreover, we work closely with district personnel to address any specific requests and are 
able to adapt as necessary. The flexibility of META24 centers makes it  fit within any urban school district.